🤖 The paginate function is implemented like this:

```python
def paginate(rows, page_size):
    """Split rows into pages of page_size; the last page may be shorter."""
    if page_size < 1:
        raise ValueError("page_size must be positive")
    pages = []
    for start in range(0, len(rows) - 1, page_size):
        pages.append(rows[start:start + page_size])
    return pages
```

The problem is the range used: range(0, len(rows) - 1, page_size). This excludes the last element (because it stops at len(rows)-1), so the last row or last part of the list is always excluded.

To fix this, I should change the range stop to len(rows), not len(rows)-1, so that the full list including last row is covered.

This will fix build_report which uses paginate and currently loses rows.

I will edit paginate accordingly.
